From e1176b746c9a4ee8df348c2ed6e348dd3b96f144 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sunwoong Joo <gomida@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 20:22:50 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 4/8] headless: renderer CaptureAgent for the prepare step
 (wake, media quiescence, markers)

Patch 6 of the deterministic capture series. Every frame in a
--deterministic-capture renderer gets a CaptureAgent (associated mojo
interface, headless/public/mojom/capture_agent.mojom). After the virtual-time
grant and before the BeginFrame, CaptureSession calls Prepare(): the agent
round-trips the media and compositor threads so due work runs now, waits with
media-thread round trips until no WebMediaPlayerImpl has a pipeline operation
in flight (bounded by media.waitTimeoutMs; media.failOnWaitTimeout chooses
error or warning), flushes the media element event queues so canplay/ended
handlers run before the main frame, and collects performance.mark entries
with the configured prefix from an isolated world. Marks are attributed to
frames by age (a mark made in frame n-1's rAF belongs to n-1). advance
responses now carry markers, media states, prepare/wake/quiesce timings and
warnings; features markers and prepare are advertised.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
